--------------------------------------------------------------------------
fancy-regex (vendored, with a Synsema patch)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
engine/vendor/fancy-regex contains the source of the fancy-regex crate,
version 0.20.2 (https://github.com/fancy-regex/fancy-regex), with a patch
by the Synsema project: a step budget for searches, a limit for the size
of a compiled pattern and of its search caches, and fixes to what a
capture group, a case-insensitive backreference, a repetition that can
match empty, an alternation and a conditional with two empty branches
match, to the number a capture group gets after a DEFINE block or beside
a repetition of zero times, and to how quantifiers and their counts are
read; a capture group in a look-behind of variable length, which was
read in more than one way, is an error. What changes and why is in
engine/vendor/fancy-regex/SYNSEMA.md; the patch itself is
engine/vendor/fancy-regex/synsema.patch. It is the engine of the
backtrack_* builtins.

